{"term":"doubt","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d2c1de4e2f4e4a040a","definition":"To consider questionable or unlikely; to hesitate to believe; to lack confidence in; to question.","example":"He doubted that was really what you meant.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["distrust","mistrust"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["doubtable","doubter","doubting","doubtingly","doubting Thomas","doubting Thomasina","I doubt it","undoubted","undoubtedly","undoubting","undoubtingly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5d7953eaff4cf1e0cd","definition":"To harbour suspicion about; suspect.","example":"I walk by the Rule of my Maſter, you walk by the rude working of your fancies. You are counted thieves already, by the Lord of the way; therefore, I doubt you will not be found true men at the end of the way.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["doubtable","doubter","doubting","doubtingly","doubting Thomas","doubting Thomasina","I doubt it","undoubted","undoubtedly","undoubting","undoubtingly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:77b02118a252a879c8","definition":"To anticipate with dread or fear; to apprehend.","example":"The rest of his horsemen the Duke sent to his campe, bicause they heard a great noise there, and doubted the enimies sally, and indeede they had issued foorth thrise, but were alwaies repulsed, especially through the valiantns of the English men that the Duke left there behind him [...]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["doubtable","doubter","doubting","doubtingly","doubting Thomas","doubting Thomasina","I doubt it","undoubted","undoubtedly","undoubting","undoubtingly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:99e35e3fbabafff33d","definition":"To fill with fear; to affright.","example":"I'll tell ye all my fears, one ſingle valour, / the vertues of the valiant Caratach / more doubts me then all Britain: [...]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["doubtable","doubter","doubting","doubtingly","doubting Thomas","doubting Thomasina","I doubt it","undoubted","undoubtedly","undoubting","undoubtingly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5fff59fc7ba1f971c0","definition":"To dread, to fear.","example":"Edmond aþelstones broþer · after him was king · / Godmon & doutede · god þoru alle þing ·","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, obsolete","register":"ambitransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["doubtable","doubter","doubting","doubtingly","doubting Thomas","doubting Thomasina","I doubt it","undoubted","undoubtedly","undoubting","undoubtingly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea2f3b456a9db9cf1b","definition":"Disbelief or uncertainty (about something); (countable) a particular instance of such disbelief or uncertainty.","example":"There was some doubt as to who the child's real father was.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["incertitude"],"antonyms":["belief","confidence","faith"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncoun